{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017sA55hTw8KQX8VKLbeyS27","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Supabase docs Row Level Security\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Securing your API\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/api/securing-your-api\"},{\"title\":\"Securing your data\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/secure-data\"},{\"title\":\"Database\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/overview\"},{\"title\":\"RAG with Permissions\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/ai/rag-with-permissions\"},{\"title\":\"Tables and data\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/tables\"},{\"title\":\"API keys\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/getting-started/api-keys\"},{\"title\":\"Auth\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth\"},{\"title\":\"Production Checklist\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/deployment/going-into-prod\"},{\"title\":\"Supabase Docs\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/troubleshooting/storage-error-403-forbidden-new-row-violates-row-level-security-policy-on-upload-a94384\"},{\"title\":\"Realtime Authorization\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/realtime/authorization\"}]\n\nThe Supabase docs cover Row Level Security (RLS) across several pages. The main points:\n\n- **Core guides:** The main RLS reference sits under the Database \"Access and security\" section, with separate pages for performance and column-level security. [3-8]\n- **Enabling RLS:** Tables made in the Dashboard have RLS turned on automatically, but tables created with SQL need it enabled manually. [5-5, 5-6] Until a policy exists, Data API requests return no rows. [5-10]\n- **Grants vs. policies:** Grants decide which roles can reach an object, while RLS decides which rows those roles can see or change. Both are needed for every exposed object. [1-7, 1-10, 1-13]\n- **Key roles:** Publishable keys resolve to the `anon` or `authenticated` role depending on whether a user is signed in. Secret keys use `service_role`, which bypasses RLS. [6-11, 6-12]\n- **Common pitfalls:** Postgres checks grants before RLS, so a missing grant produces a permission error, while a policy matching no rows returns an empty result. [6-13, 6-15] Storage uploads can also fail with a 403 if the table lacks a SELECT policy. [9-6]\n- **Realtime:** Realtime authorization uses RLS policies on the `realtime.messages` table. [10-5]\n\nThe most useful starting points are the main \"Row Level Security\" guide and the \"Securing your API\" page, which covers grants and RLS together.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a993cec-e7b1-4ce4-abd3-b1d8c09597d5","uuid":"193f818b-e94c-4c82-b6e5-d031362f956b","timestamp":"2026-10-16T23:11:47.894Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Supabase docs Row Level Security","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_0147wfrc6uc4SoJAQu2mZuHr","content":[{"title":"Securing your API","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/api/securing-your-api"},{"title":"Securing your data","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/secure-data"},{"title":"Database","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/overview"},{"title":"RAG with Permissions","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/ai/rag-with-permissions"},{"title":"Tables and data","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/tables"},{"title":"API keys","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/getting-started/api-keys"},{"title":"Auth","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth"},{"title":"Production Checklist","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/deployment/going-into-prod"},{"title":"Supabase Docs","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/troubleshooting/storage-error-403-forbidden-new-row-violates-row-level-security-policy-on-upload-a94384"},{"title":"Realtime Authorization","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/realtime/authorization"}]},"The Supabase docs cover Row Level Security (RLS) across several pages. The main points:\n\n- **Core guides:** The main RLS reference sits under the Database \"Access and security\" section, with separate pages for performance and column-level security. [3-8]\n- **Enabling RLS:** Tables made in the Dashboard have RLS turned on automatically, but tables created with SQL need it enabled manually. [5-5, 5-6] Until a policy exists, Data API requests return no rows. [5-10]\n- **Grants vs. policies:** Grants decide which roles can reach an object, while RLS decides which rows those roles can see or change. Both are needed for every exposed object. [1-7, 1-10, 1-13]\n- **Key roles:** Publishable keys resolve to the `anon` or `authenticated` role depending on whether a user is signed in. Secret keys use `service_role`, which bypasses RLS. [6-11, 6-12]\n- **Common pitfalls:** Postgres checks grants before RLS, so a missing grant produces a permission error, while a policy matching no rows returns an empty result. [6-13, 6-15] Storage uploads can also fail with a 403 if the table lacks a SELECT policy. [9-6]\n- **Realtime:** Realtime authorization uses RLS policies on the `realtime.messages` table. [10-5]\n\nThe most useful starting points are the main \"Row Level Security\" guide and the \"Securing your API\" page, which covers grants and RLS together."],"durationSeconds":4.968278519000001,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017sA55hTw8KQX8VKLbeyS27","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
